34,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My findings were quite concerning; the site diaries show significant time lost to weather, and the older blocks contain hazardous materials that have caused previous projects to slip by months.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found that general-purpose rooms are in high demand all year, while specialist rooms are often idle, and taking rooms out of service has cost us a lot in off-site rentals.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"It appears the burden is uneven; while some technicians have spare hours, the grounds and front-of-house posts remain unfilled, and bench technicians are wasting time on manual tasks the equipment should handle.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The post-occupancy reviews show that projects benefiting the whole campus are rated highest, while the delivery schedules reveal that comfort-based projects often slip by a year or more.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My research confirms a financial disconnect; mechanical plant costs are rising sharply while surfacing remains stable, and we have completely failed to set aside reserves for replacing old audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,It seems we are facing a pattern where unforeseen physical obstacles and weather delays are pushing our timelines back significantly. We must be very careful about what we commit to.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, that's true, but we also can't ignore that we're paying for off-site space because we lack general rooms. Maybe we should prioritize something that solves that demand?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"I must point out that any new facility will require maintenance. If we ignore the fact that our grounds staff is depleted and technicians are bogged down by outdated equipment, we are only adding to the burden.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that is a valid point. However, we must also consider that projects focused on general utility and campus-wide access are the ones that actually satisfy the users and tend to be more successful.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is fascinating how our findings converge. We have rising costs for mechanical systems, a lack of AV reserves, and a history of delays for ""comfort"" projects. We must avoid a costly, slipping vanity project.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I wonder if we should prioritize a project that avoids the older blocks and outdoor exposure, as those seem to be the primary sources of our scheduling nightmares.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, that makes sense! If we can find a project that doesn't involve hazardous materials or rain delays, we can actually get it finished on time for the students!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I would argue that we must also prioritize a project that reduces the manual workload for our technicians, rather than one that simply adds more equipment for them to maintain.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that is a fair concern. If we can find a project that balances high user demand with a low risk of delivery failure and minimal staffing strain, that would be the ideal choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. We should seek a solution that is financially predictable and avoids the pitfalls of mechanical inflation or the absence of AV funding, lest we find ourselves in another budgetary vacuum.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I believe we have a very clear set of criteria now. We need a project that is low-risk regarding weather and hazardous materials, and one that serves the wider community.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I agree! And it should definitely be something that addresses the shortage of general-purpose rooms so we can stop spending so much on those expensive off-site rentals.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I will support any plan that alleviates the current manual burden on our technical staff, as we cannot simply keep asking the same few people to do more.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. We need a project that is highly rated by users, avoids the ""comfort"" trap that leads to delays, and doesn't create an unsustainable maintenance burden for our staff.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I concur. Let us hope the candidates provide a choice that is as fiscally disciplined as it is practical, avoiding the siren song of expensive mechanical upgrades we cannot afford.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
