60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Now that we have the candidates, I see the Campus Path Network involves outdoor work and the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade involves the older blocks; both seem quite risky for our schedule.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with @Shizue! The Central Study Commons sounds perfect because it turns an underused hall into general study space, which is exactly what the booking data says we need.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade would certainly help the bench technicians by automating those manual routines, but I worry about the staffing gaps in other areas.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The Media Production Center relies on AV equipment, which @Benjamin noted lacks a renewal reserve, and the Study Commons aligns with the high ratings for campus-wide, bookable spaces.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I must agree with Mizuki. The Media Production Center is a financial trap without a renewal reserve, and the Ventilation Upgrade's mechanical costs are likely to spiral. The Study Commons is the most fiscally sound.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Benjamin and Mizuki. The Central Study Commons avoids the hazardous materials of the labs and the weather risks of the paths, making it the safest choice for our timeline.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,It's a win-win! We get more general-purpose rooms for the students and we avoid those expensive off-site rentals. I'm fully in favor of the Central Study Commons!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"While the ventilation upgrade would solve the technicians' immediate struggle, I cannot ignore the risks @Shizue mentioned. If the project slips, the staff will be under even more pressure. I will support the Study Commons.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have reached a consensus. The Central Study Commons satisfies the demand for general-purpose space, avoids the risks of delivery failure, and remains financially sustainable.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare occasion that we find a candidate that satisfies the logistical, financial, and human constraints simultaneously. I believe the Central Study Commons is the only rational choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am quite happy that we have found a solution that considers everyone's concerns. I shall cast my vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for the Central Study Commons too! It's the best way to help the students and the budget!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"I will also cast my vote for the Central Study Commons, as it is the most responsible path forward for our staff and students.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I shall also vote for the Central Study Commons, as it is the most logical choice based on the evidence we have gathered.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall join the consensus and cast my vote for the Central Study Commons; it is the only option that avoids a fiscal or logistical catastrophe.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
